module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.directory_ownership_assertion_stops_at_the_top_level

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, Recurrence, Witnessed }

// THE ROW: an ownership assertion that stops at the directory it names.
//
// THE SHAPE, in the abstract: a provider declares "this directory is owned by U:G, group-writable,
// setgid" and reads as though it had said "everything under this directory". It has not. The assert is
// one chgrp and one chmod on one inode, and the tree beneath it keeps whatever it already had. The
// defect is invisible at the moment the apply succeeds -- the declared directory reads back exactly as
// demanded, receipted, correct -- and appears only when something arrives that has to write a PATH
// UNDERNEATH rather than the directory itself.
//
// WHERE IT BIT, and how it was mistaken for something else: WORKER-ROOT-EQUIVALENT-2 (#14270) declared
// .git/objects, .git/refs and .git/logs group-writable setgid for the shared attempt group so a
// dedicated worker could commit into the lab instance's repository. The apply passed. srv1 then read
// the actual repository (2026-10-17, gunbc-worker 1004/1004 and gunbc-attempt 1003 created exactly as
// fleet_posix_accounts declares) and found objects, refs, logs AND their existing subdirectories --
// .git/objects/f9 among them -- still briansrls:briansrls 0775. The worker, not being in that group,
// could not write into the fan-out directory its own object belonged in, and its first commit died
// inside it. The natural reading was "the account is wrong" or "the group membership is wrong"; neither
// was, both had been checked. The grant was right about the directory and silent about the tree.
//
// THE GENERALIZATION, which is what belongs in the ledger: a group-writable setgid directory makes
// what is created NEXT inherit the group. It says nothing about what is ALREADY there, and git
// repositories, caches, spool directories and build trees are never empty at the moment a second
// principal is introduced to them. So any grant introduced to an EXISTING tree needs two claims and
// only ever gets one: the directory, and the contents. The contents half has to be a separate,
// BOUNDED step -- bounded depth, confined names pruned, symlinks excluded, one group and never an
// owner -- because a recursive assert over a tree that grows is a step whose cost nobody declared.
//
// HOW THE LEDGER CLOSES IT: the same claims read both halves, and the pre-migration state is stated in
// the model as the thing the readback REFUSES (dashboard_git_worker_directory_mode_is_unmigrated), so
// "it passed on srv1" cannot be re-mistaken for "it is granted".
fn row() -> RecurringFailureMode {
  RecurringFailureMode {
    name: "directory ownership assertion stops at the top level" as NonEmptyStr,
    bad_thought: "the directory is declared group-writable setgid, so the tree under it is group-writable setgid" as NonEmptyStr,
    reality: "the assert is one chgrp and one chmod on one inode: existing contents keep their owner, their group and their mode, and the new writer fails on the first path UNDERNEATH the granted directory. What is created next inherits the group; what is already there does not." as NonEmptyStr,
    detection: "read back a DESCENDANT, not just the declared directory -- an existing subdirectory's mode and group, where the second principal has to write. If only the declared path is receipted, the assertion is top-level and the tree is unclaimed." as NonEmptyStr,
    prevention: "the grant ships with a declared, BOUNDED migration over the existing subtree (depth cap, confined names pruned by name, symlinks excluded, group only -- never an owner) whose READBACK the model itself checks; and where the writer creates directories, setgid on directories only, so the next fan-out directory is born in the right group." as NonEmptyStr,
    recurrence: Witnessed {
      count: 1 as NonEmptyStr,
      first_refusal: "the lab worker's first commit: 'index.lock'/'objects/f9/...': Permission denied with .git/objects correctly 02775 and its existing fan-out directories 0775 briansrls:briansrls (WORKER-ROOT-EQUIVALENT-3, srv1 2026-10-17)" as NonEmptyStr,
    } as Recurrence,
    claim: decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.roadmap.worker_dedicated_account_witness", decl_name: "the_existing_subtree_is_covered_by_the_declared_migration" as NonEmptyStr),
  }
}
